  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-07T12:19:20.649Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It is difficult to use the new Action Menu because of controller drift on my joysticks.\n\nThe emote tab should still be an option in the Quick Menu.\n\nThe long menu button press for the Action Menu keeps getting in the way for playspace mover/elsewhere. An option to turn that off would be appreciated.\n\nBy using a pointer system with the Quick Menu, it would be easier to use sliders and hit buttons without the probability of misclicking by pushing the joystick a slightly wrong direction. Joysticks feel a bit slippery and the trackpad with vive wands felt really slippery.\n\nAlso, if the Action Menu is opened, movement doesn't turn it off. I find myself hitting actions by accident when trying to use the occupied joystick when the Action Menu is on.",
